WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.795
Attempting to rescue the young widow would be a bold undertaking, maybe even an impossible one.

2
00:00:06.796 --> 00:00:12.522
But Mr. Fogg did not hesitate, and Sir Francis was an enthusiastic ally.

3
00:00:12.523 --> 00:00:18.232
Passepartout was ready for anything, and even the guide was on their side.

4
00:00:18.233 --> 00:00:21.602
"Where are they taking her?" asked Mr. Fogg.

5
00:00:21.603 --> 00:00:26.135
"To the pagoda of Pillaji, two miles from here," said the guide.

6
00:00:26.136 --> 00:00:32.307
"The woman will spend the night there, and the sacrifice will take place at the first light of dawn."

7
00:00:32.308 --> 00:00:36.062
The guide looked at the group of rescuers.

8
00:00:36.063 --> 00:00:43.346
"It is certain that we shall risk not only our lives but horrible tortures if we are caught!"

9
00:00:43.347 --> 00:00:50.772
"That is foreseen," said Mr. Fogg. "I think we must wait until night before acting."

10
00:00:50.773 --> 00:00:53.927
"I agree," said Sir Francis.

11
00:00:53.928 --> 00:00:57.184
Their guide gave an account of the woman.

12
00:00:57.185 --> 00:01:03.637
"She is the daughter of a wealthy Bombay merchant and received an excellent English education.

13
00:01:03.638 --> 00:01:12.918
Her name is Aouda. While still very young, she was left an orphan and was married against her will to an old rajah.

14
00:01:12.919 --> 00:01:17.614
When he died, she escaped, knowing the fate that awaited her.

15
00:01:17.615 --> 00:01:23.235
But she was captured. That is why she is under such heavy guard now."

16
00:01:23.236 --> 00:01:29.040
The guide’s story strengthened the determination of Mr. Fogg and his friends.

17
00:01:29.041 --> 00:01:34.396
As soon as night fell, the guide led them deeper into the thick jungle.

18
00:01:34.397 --> 00:01:37.026
They came to an area lit by torches.

19
00:01:37.027 --> 00:01:43.124
A group of Indians were sleeping outside a wide brick wall that enclosed the tall pagoda. Guards

20
00:01:43.125 --> 00:01:47.811
with swords marched back and forth before the doors. The

21
00:01:47.812 --> 00:01:52.831
rescuers hid themselves and waited, hoping the guards would fall asleep. After

22
00:01:52.832 --> 00:02:01.074
midnight, when it was clear that the guards were going to patrol all night, Fogg and his companions sneaked around to the back of the pagoda. With

23
00:02:01.075 --> 00:02:08.750
two sturdy knives that their guide had brought, Mr. Fogg and Sir Francis worked quietly at the loose bricks of the wall. They

24
00:02:08.751 --> 00:02:14.760
managed to dislodge a few and then found they could remove the other bricks with their hands. Their

25
00:02:14.761 --> 00:02:19.422
plan was to open a hole large enough for Aouda to slip through. Suddenly

26
00:02:19.423 --> 00:02:23.158
a cry arose from inside the pagoda. Mr.

27
00:02:23.159 --> 00:02:29.318
Fogg and his friends escaped into the jungle just as the guards ran to the back of the pagoda. Sir

28
00:02:29.319 --> 00:02:35.955
Francis shook his fists, Passepartout was furious, and the guide grimaced with rage. How

29
00:02:35.956 --> 00:02:42.199
could they save Aouda now? The tranquil Mr. Fogg waited, revealing no emotion. "We

30
00:02:42.200 --> 00:02:47.204
can do nothing but go on our way," whispered Sir Francis. "He

31
00:02:47.205 --> 00:02:51.040
is right. We must go," said the guide. "Stop,"

32
00:02:51.041 --> 00:02:57.059
said Fogg. "I am not due at Allahabad before noon tomorrow. We

33
